ot flow forward in time. Constrained (<=600) reachability from 1385 reaches only 2 nodes and never 1186; even unconstrained temporal search reaches 340 nodes but not 1186, and no temporal paths are found. A static path does exist through hub 639 and 1818, and the surrounding nodes are busy throughout the window, which explains the apparent connection without any genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings:**\n\n- Node 1385 has exactly 1 event in the window (out to hub 639); node 1186 has exactly 1 event (in from 1818) \u2014 step_02, step_07, step_06.\n- Timing: 1385's only event falls in bin [71149, 75948]; 1186's only event falls in the *earlier* bin [66349, 71148] (step_13, step_14). The target's only contact precedes the source's only contact, so no time-respecting sequence can exist.\n- Constrained reachability (max_wait 600) reaches only 2 nodes and fails (step_03, step_12); even with **no** waiting constraint, 340 nodes are reached but 1186 is not (step_04), and no temporal paths exist (step_15) \u2014 ruling out the \"static connection exists\" explanation (1385\u2013639\u2013\u2026\u20131818\u20131186 is connected when time is ignored, step_05/step_09/step_10).\n- Volume is not the issue: the 1385/639/1818/1186 group is active throughout the window (step_11), and the graph has 5,532 events (step_01) \u2014 activity is ample, ordering is what fails.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1385 and 1186 each participate in exactly one interaction in the window: 1385->639 (~71-76k) and 1818->1186 (~66-71k). The target's only contact happens before the source's, so influence cannot flow forward in time. Constrained (<=600) reachability from 1385 reaches only 2 nodes and never 1186; even unconstrained temporal search reaches 340 nodes but not 1186, and no temporal paths are found. A static path does exist through hub 639 and 1818, and the surrounding nodes are busy throughout the window, which explains the apparent connection without any genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 41763, "total_output_tokens": 3368, "total_tokens": 45131, "total_latency_ms": 50011, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}